WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.307
One beautiful October morning, Marilla and Anne sat in the kitchen and cut vegetables.

2
00:00:09.308 --> 00:00:15.599
"Anne," Marilla began, "why don't you ask Diana to come over for afternoon tea?

3
00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:18.679
I am going into town, and she can come then."

4
00:00:18.680 --> 00:00:24.465
"Oh, Marilla!" Anne clasped her hands. "How perfectly lovely!

5
00:00:24.466 --> 00:00:29.635
We will be like grown-ups! Can we use the teapot with the roses?"

6
00:00:29.636 --> 00:00:36.225
"No, but I have some cake and raspberry cordial in the pantry you can have," Marilla replied.

7
00:00:36.226 --> 00:00:40.327
Diana came over, dressed in her second-best dress.

8
00:00:40.328 --> 00:00:46.684
Anne, dressed in her own second-best dress, opened the door with a very serious expression.

9
00:00:46.685 --> 00:00:49.134
Together they went to the front room.

10
00:00:49.135 --> 00:00:52.912
"How is your mother?" Anne asked politely, like an adult.

11
00:00:52.913 --> 00:00:59.232
"She is very well, thank you. And Mr. Cuthbert is in the potato fields?" asked Diana.

12
00:00:59.233 --> 00:01:05.279
"Yes, he is. Our potatoes are very good this year," replied Anne.

13
00:01:05.280 --> 00:01:12.638
Abruptly her tone changed. "Oh Diana!" she burst out. "Let's go and pick some apples!"

14
00:01:12.639 --> 00:01:18.901
The girls instantly stopped acting like proper ladies and ran outside to the apple orchard.

15
00:01:18.902 --> 00:01:22.916
"Marilla said we can pick the rest of the apples," said Anne.

16
00:01:22.917 --> 00:01:29.552
"Marilla is very kind. She also said we can have cake and raspberry cordial for tea.

17
00:01:29.553 --> 00:01:34.188
I love red drinks—they just taste better, don't they?"

18
00:01:34.189 --> 00:01:40.128
Later the girls went inside, and Anne went to the pantry to get the raspberry cordial.

19
00:01:40.129 --> 00:01:45.108
At first she couldn't see it anywhere, but then she spotted it at the back.

20
00:01:45.109 --> 00:01:48.562
Anne put the cordial on the table with a big glass.

21
00:01:48.563 --> 00:01:54.046
"Please help yourself, Diana. I can't drink a thing after eating all those apples."

22
00:01:54.047 --> 00:01:57.807
Diana poured herself some of the drink and sipped it.

23
00:01:57.808 --> 00:02:01.283
"This is a very nice cordial, Anne," she said.

24
00:02:01.284 --> 00:02:04.261
"I didn't know cordial tasted so good."

25
00:02:04.262 --> 00:02:10.642
"I'm glad you like it," Anne replied. "Take as much as you want. I'll get the cake."

26
00:02:10.643 --> 00:02:15.219
When Anne came back, Diana was drinking a second glass of cordial.

27
00:02:15.220 --> 00:02:19.311
Diana started to drink a third glass, and Anne didn't mind.

28
00:02:19.312 --> 00:02:23.339
"It's the nicest cordial I ever drank," said Diana.

29
00:02:23.340 --> 00:02:29.379
"It's much nicer than Mrs. Lynde's cordial. It doesn't taste a bit like hers."

30
00:02:29.380 --> 00:02:34.797
"I'm sure Marilla's cordial is nicer than Mrs. Lynde's," said Anne loyally.

31
00:02:34.798 --> 00:02:41.453
"Marilla is a famous cook. She's trying to teach me, but it's hard work, Diana.

32
00:02:41.454 --> 00:02:48.192
"Last week," Anne continued, "Marilla told me to put some pudding sauce in the pantry and cover it.

33
00:02:48.193 --> 00:02:52.770
I took the bowl of sauce into the pantry, but I forgot to cover it.

34
00:02:52.771 --> 00:02:56.116
I remembered the next morning and ran to the pantry.

35
00:02:56.117 --> 00:03:00.176
Diana, a mouse had drowned in the sauce!

36
00:03:00.177 --> 00:03:03.700
I used a spoon to get the mouse and took it outside.

37
00:03:03.701 --> 00:03:07.371
"Then I was going to tell Marilla about the mouse.

38
00:03:07.372 --> 00:03:15.036
But I started pretending I was a forest fairy flying through the trees, and I forgot about the mouse and the sauce.

39
00:03:15.037 --> 00:03:18.760
After that Mr. and Mrs. Ross came for lunch.

40
00:03:18.761 --> 00:03:26.843
We ate lunch and everything was fine until I saw Marilla coming in with plum pudding and pudding sauce, warmed up.

41
00:03:26.844 --> 00:03:33.695
I remembered everything and shouted, 'Marilla, don't use the sauce. A mouse drowned in it!'

42
00:03:33.696 --> 00:03:38.675
Mr. and Mrs. Ross looked at me, and I thought I would die!

43
00:03:38.676 --> 00:03:44.524
"Why, Diana," Anne said suddenly. "What's the matter?"

44
00:03:44.525 --> 00:03:49.442
Diana stood up and then sat down, putting her hands to her head.

45
00:03:49.443 --> 00:03:56.407
"I'm . . . I'm very sick," she said. "I . . . I must go home."

46
00:03:56.408 --> 00:04:00.899
"No, don't go yet. You must eat some cake first." "I

47
00:04:00.900 --> 00:04:04.086
must go home," Diana repeated. "Where

48
00:04:04.087 --> 00:04:06.849
do you feel bad?" Anne asked. "I'm

49
00:04:06.850 --> 00:04:10.350
very dizzy," said Diana. Anne

50
00:04:10.351 --> 00:04:15.313
was very disappointed, but she took Diana to the Barrys' fence. The

51
00:04:15.314 --> 00:04:20.046
next day Marilla sent Anne to Mrs. Lynde's house on an errand. In

52
00:04:20.047 --> 00:04:25.689
a short space of time, Anne came flying back to Green Gables in tears. "What's

53
00:04:25.690 --> 00:04:28.728
the matter, Anne?" Marilla said. "Mrs.

54
00:04:28.729 --> 00:04:36.311
Lynde saw Diana's mother today. Mrs. Barry said that I sent Diana home drunk. And

55
00:04:36.312 --> 00:04:44.956
she said I was a very wicked girl and she's never, never going to let Diana play with me again!" "Diana

56
00:04:44.957 --> 00:04:54.240
was drunk?" Marilla was stunned. "Anne, are you or Mrs. Barry crazy? What did you give her?" "Nothing

57
00:04:54.241 --> 00:05:03.969
but raspberry cordial," Anne said. "I never thought it made you drunk, not even if you drink three glasses like Diana did." Marilla

58
00:05:03.970 --> 00:05:09.555
marched to the pantry. On the shelf was a bottle of homemade wine. At

59
00:05:09.556 --> 00:05:17.449
that moment Marilla remembered that the cordial was in the cellar and not the pantry as she had told Anne. Marilla

60
00:05:17.450 --> 00:05:23.717
went back into the kitchen. "Anne, you gave Diana wine instead of cordial! Don't

61
00:05:23.718 --> 00:05:26.056
you know the difference between them?" "I

62
00:05:26.057 --> 00:05:31.712
didn't taste the drink," said Anne. "Only Diana drank it. And

63
00:05:31.713 --> 00:05:35.450
then Diana got so sick and went home. Mrs.

64
00:05:35.451 --> 00:05:43.667
Barry said Diana just laughed and laughed, and then slept for hours, and had a headache all day. Her

65
00:05:43.668 --> 00:05:47.946
mother smelled her breath and knew she was drunk." "Three

66
00:05:47.947 --> 00:05:52.834
glasses of cordial would make you sick," Marilla said, troubled. "But

67
00:05:52.835 --> 00:05:57.678
it was an accident, Anne, so don't worry. I'll talk to Mrs. Barry." At

68
00:05:57.679 --> 00:06:02.506
that, Marilla left. When she came back later, she was frowning. "Was

69
00:06:02.507 --> 00:06:06.448
Mrs. Barry still angry?" asked Anne. "Mrs.

70
00:06:06.449 --> 00:06:13.589
Barry?" snapped Marilla. "I told her it was a mistake, but she didn't believe me. So

71
00:06:13.590 --> 00:06:22.137
I told her that if my girl was so greedy, drinking three glasses of anything, I'd be punishing her! "

72
00:06:22.138 --> 00:06:29.797
Marilla went into the kitchen. Anne stepped outside, and she walked determinedly to the Barrys' house and knocked on the door.

73
00:06:29.798 --> 00:06:36.714
When Mrs. Barry saw it was Anne, she frowned. "What do you want?" she demanded.

74
00:06:36.715 --> 00:06:42.395
Anne clasped her hands. "Oh, Mrs. Barry, please forgive me.

75
00:06:42.396 --> 00:06:48.834
I did not mean to . . . to make Diana . . . drunk. How could I?

76
00:06:48.835 --> 00:06:54.330
She is my best friend in the world. I thought it was raspberry cordial.

77
00:06:54.331 --> 00:06:57.479
Please say that you'll let me play with Diana.

78
00:06:57.480 --> 00:07:04.774
If I can't play with her, my life will be covered by a huge dark cloud of sadness."

79
00:07:04.775 --> 00:07:08.767
Anne's dramatic plea had no effect on Mrs. Barry.

80
00:07:08.768 --> 00:07:12.697
She said coldly, "Anne, you should go home.

81
00:07:12.698 --> 00:07:16.301
You are not a good friend for Diana."

82
00:07:16.302 --> 00:07:22.173
"Can't I see Diana and just say one last good-bye?" Anne asked.

83
00:07:22.174 --> 00:07:27.085
"Diana is out with her father," said Mrs. Barry, shutting the door.

84
00:07:27.086 --> 00:07:30.689
Anne walked back to Green Gables with her head down.

85
00:07:30.690 --> 00:07:36.159
"My last hope is gone," she told Marilla, full of despair.

86
00:07:36.160 --> 00:07:40.952
"I talked to Mrs. Barry, and she treated me very badly.

87
00:07:40.953 --> 00:07:43.946
I can do nothing now but pray.

88
00:07:43.947 --> 00:07:51.139
But I don't think that will help because even God can't change Mrs. Barry's mind."

89
00:07:51.140 --> 00:07:57.726
"Anne, don't talk like that," said Marilla, trying not to laugh at Anne's theatrics.

90
00:07:57.727 --> 00:08:05.418
But later Marilla couldn't help feeling pity for Anne when she saw that the child had cried herself to sleep.

91
00:08:05.419 --> 00:08:15.832
"Poor little thing," Marilla whispered, kissing Anne's red cheek.

